        "original_id": "3565e875-a090-5b6f-9a04-2ac853914e85",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Gin Drinkers Line, Hong Kong\n- Events: Battle of Hong Kong, Pacific War, World War II\n- Organizations: British military, Japanese forces\n\nFacts:\n- The Battle of Hong Kong took place from 8 to 25 December 1941 and was one of the first battles of the Pacific War in World War II.\n- The Battle of Hong Kong was also known as the Defence of Hong Kong and the Fall of Hong Kong.\n- The Gin Drinkers Line was a British military defensive line in Hong Kong against the Japanese invasion during the Battle of Hong Kong in December 1941.\n- The Gin Drinkers Line was also called the Gin Drinkers' Line.",
